  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** AVITA is transitioning from a burn-focused single-product company to a diversified wound-care platform, with new offerings like RECELL GO, Cohealyx, and PermeaDerm broadening its addressable market into trauma and soft-tissue repair. The narrative shows early international momentum following CE Mark approval in Europe, while U.S. revenue remains heavily concentrated in a few hundred burn centers. Product mix shifts are weighing on gross margins, and a previously flagged liquidity overhang persists despite a resolved reimbursement issue. A recent clinical data catalyst for Cohealyx triggered a sharp but fragile share-price bounce, with thin institutional conviction highlighting ongoing micro-cap risk.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is pursuing a high-stakes turnaround centered on cost discipline, portfolio diversification, and geographic expansion. They have reduced operating expenses, addressed the prior reimbursement bottleneck, and steered the business toward higher-volume trauma and wound-care settings. The strategic pivot is underway, yet execution credibility remains under scrutiny: the market’s tepid institutional participation following positive news suggests that rebuilding confidence will require consistent commercial traction and a durable resolution of balance-sheet fragility.",
